## Scientific workflow

The application is intended to:
1. inspect preliminary CM1 NetCDF output files
2. identify relevant coordinates and atmospheric variables
3. detect storm updraft and vertical-vorticity regions
4. track feature centroids across time
5. estimate storm motion from linear or rolling regressions
6. compare one-run and two-run analyses
7. export results and a CM1 namelist recommendation

## Known limitations

This scaffold is intentionally not a fake placeholder. It includes real numerical logic for the core math and tracking steps, but it is still a foundation rather than a fully field-tested production release. The following items are planned next:
- full GUI controls for simulation loading and settings
- richer time-window filtering and analysis dialogs
- more rigorous staggered-grid interpolation handling
- robust multi-run comparison logic
- CSV/text export and namelist recommendation generation
- validation against real CM1 r22.0 datasets

## Testing

```bash
pytest
```

## Development notes

This project follows an incremental development approach and keeps the analysis code independent from the GUI so it can be tested separately.

